WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.200 --> 00:00:02.300
-Guys, let's do a couple
thank-you notes.

00:00:02.300 --> 00:00:03.734
You guys, is that okay?
Let's --

00:00:03.734 --> 00:00:05.734
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:07.767 --> 00:00:09.467
[ Piano plays ]

00:00:09.467 --> 00:00:12.767
Thank you, last week of January.

00:00:12.767 --> 00:00:16.400
Or as all my resolutions put it,
"Well, there's always 2023."

00:00:16.400 --> 00:00:18.234
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:18.234 --> 00:00:19.467
Do it next year.

00:00:19.467 --> 00:00:22.267
-Come on, man.
Don't be so hard on yourself.

00:00:22.267 --> 00:00:23.868
[ Piano plays ]

00:00:23.868 --> 00:00:28.601
-Thank you, bomb cyclone, for
sounding less like a snowstorm

00:00:28.601 --> 00:00:32.434
and more like what happens when
you pour 151 in a McFlurry.

00:00:32.434 --> 00:00:34.601
[ Laughter and applause ]
That's my jam.

00:00:34.601 --> 00:00:37.000
-[ Slurps ]

00:00:37.000 --> 00:00:38.767
[ Smacks lips ]

00:00:38.767 --> 00:00:40.868
[ Piano plays ]

00:00:40.868 --> 00:00:44.567
-Thank you, meteorologist who
said this weekend's winter storm

00:00:44.567 --> 00:00:48.934
could bring snow anywhere
between 2 and 20 inches.

00:00:48.934 --> 00:00:50.767
[ Laughter ]

00:00:53.100 --> 00:00:56.234
Or as the guy who's coming
to install my cable put it,

00:00:56.234 --> 00:00:58.634
the student
has become the master.

00:00:58.634 --> 00:01:00.634
[ Applause ]

00:01:04.033 --> 00:01:07.000
Anywhere between
2 and 20 inches.

00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:08.901
Okay.
Thank you for nothing.

00:01:08.901 --> 00:01:10.133
Thank you for nothing.

00:01:10.133 --> 00:01:11.767
-Or 60 inches.
We just don't know.

00:01:11.767 --> 00:01:14.601
-150 inches of snow.
Or noth--

00:01:14.601 --> 00:01:17.033
Or it could be dusting,
a slight dusting.

00:01:17.033 --> 00:01:18.601
-Or it could get real hot.

00:01:18.601 --> 00:01:22.067
-It could get hot, as well.
It could, yeah.

00:01:22.067 --> 00:01:24.534
I just wanted to tell you,
give you a heads-up.

00:01:24.534 --> 00:01:25.734
-On what?

00:01:25.734 --> 00:01:26.868
-Goodbye.

00:01:26.868 --> 00:01:28.567
[ Light laughter ]

00:01:28.567 --> 00:01:30.033
[ Piano plays ]

00:01:30.033 --> 00:01:32.734
Thank you, Boris Johnson,

00:01:32.734 --> 00:01:36.968
for lying about throwing parties
during the pandemic.

00:01:36.968 --> 00:01:39.200
Though, to be fair --
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:39.200 --> 00:01:41.701
Though, to be fair, it's pretty
hard to lie about partying

00:01:41.701 --> 00:01:43.300
when you always look
like you just woke up

00:01:43.300 --> 00:01:45.534
from a three-day whiskey bender.

00:01:45.534 --> 00:01:48.534
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:48.534 --> 00:01:50.200
A little crispy today.

00:01:52.033 --> 00:01:54.501
-2 to 20?

00:01:54.501 --> 00:01:56.300
[ Piano plays ]

00:01:56.300 --> 00:01:59.834
-Thank you, Cincinnati Bengals
versus Kansas City Chiefs

00:01:59.834 --> 00:02:03.000
this weekend, or as it's known
to tailgaters,

00:02:03.000 --> 00:02:04.567
chili versus barbecue.

00:02:04.567 --> 00:02:06.133
[ Cheers and applause ]
Ah, that's right.

00:02:11.834 --> 00:02:13.634
[ Piano plays ]

00:02:13.634 --> 00:02:17.067
Thank you,
Minnie Mouse's new pantsuit,

00:02:17.067 --> 00:02:19.367
for causing
way too much controversy

00:02:19.367 --> 00:02:22.067
considering one of her friends
has never worn pants.

00:02:22.067 --> 00:02:23.634
I mean, come on.
Hey, come on.

00:02:23.634 --> 00:02:25.567
[ Applause ]
-Come on.

00:02:26.501 --> 00:02:28.334
-[ Donald Duck voice ]
I don't know.

00:02:31.634 --> 00:02:32.968
[ Piano plays ]

00:02:32.968 --> 00:02:36.601
-Thank you, metal cage
that goes around the cork,

00:02:36.601 --> 00:02:39.434
for making my prosecco feel
like it's Harry Houdini.

00:02:39.434 --> 00:02:41.200
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:42.801 --> 00:02:44.033
[ Pops lips ]

00:02:48.467 --> 00:02:53.167
Thank you, Little Caesars'
new Batman Calzony,

00:02:53.167 --> 00:02:55.367
for giving every pizza
delivery guy a great excuse

00:02:55.367 --> 00:02:57.100
for when they deliver
a crushed box.

00:02:57.100 --> 00:03:00.701
They go, "No, no,
it's the Batman Calzony."

00:03:00.701 --> 00:03:02.300
There you have it.
Those are our thank-you notes.

